            "review_title": "Review at Quan Ngu Binh",
            "review_text": "GourmandBC\nSingapore, Singapore277 contributions\n0\nConsistent authenticity - Yummy Hue Food in HCMC\nNov 2017 • Family\nBeen coming here for over 15 years. And no visit to Saigon is complete without dropping by. I must forewarn this place has a v small menu and focuses on only 8 or so dishes. It consistently sells out by 6 pm after opening at 3 pm. We often call and book in advance. Also it follows the Chinese Lunar calendar and closes on the 15 and Month end. ALL the food is stunning. The bun Beo is a must try. Steam Hue Rice cakes dressed in shredded fine shrimp and eaten w their special light fish sauce and accompanied by Cha - Vietnamese cured pork sausages. The Banh Xeo is also yummy. I love the Nem Nuong rolls with their special dipping sauce. Must must try their bun bo Hue - I always take it mixed pork trotters and beef muscle. Dread lodging this review - now it will sell out even earlier. V v v traditional place. They don’t make more they don’t have another outlet. V clean and v interesting step back into the pre war interiors.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 19, 2017",
